/E (For daily life and for athletic performance, mobility is the more relevant goal. A joint that can only achieve range of motion passively is vulnerable; a joint that can move actively through that range is strong and controllable. Most of the work in this guide develops mobility rather than passive flexibility, though both will improve together. )
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [16]
>>
